.TH WM-CAMERA 1
.SH NAME
camera \- show the camera, live
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/camera
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Camera
shows the feed at
.B /mnt/video/0
in a window, mounting
.IR camsrv (4)
there if nothing is. Holding the feed open keeps the camera on: hidden by the window
manager, or closed, it lets go, and when nothing else is reading the
camera goes off. Shown again, it takes the feed back, at the size
.B fmt
then gives: a feed turned meanwhile is shown turned.
.PP
How the camera is mounted is not the window's to say: the feed comes
the right way up from whoever started
.IR camsrv (4)
\(em its
.BR -r ,
or on a bare-metal board the card's
.B camera
file.
.PP
What is drawn over the picture is the feed's
.B layer
directory as the window's name space has it
.RI ( layers (2)):
.B bind -a
puts a layer on top,
.B bind -b
underneath, and
.B unmount
takes it off, while the window is up:
.IP
.B bind -a /mnt/vision/1/layer /mnt/video/0/layer
.PP
Frames are numbered by the feed, so each is drawn with its layers'
records for it (a detector's
.BI frame= N
on frame
.IR N ),
and their
.B frame=*
records.
.PP
Button 2 or 3 (a long press on a touch screen) is a menu:
.TF upside\ down
.TP
.B snapshot
Save the frame shown as a PNG in
.BR $home/camera ,
named by its number in the feed
.RB ( 274.png ),
and say where over the picture for two seconds.
.TP
.B rotate 90
Turn the feed a quarter turn more, clockwise (its
.BR rotate ).
.TP
.B upside down
Turn it half a turn.
.TP
.B mirror
Mirror it left to right: the sensor's mirror bit, in its
.BR flip .
.TP
.B autofocus
Focus once (a camera with a moving lens, the Camera Module 3, only).
.TP
.B exit
Close the window.
.PD
.PP
Each but snapshot is a write to the feed's
.BR ctl ,
as any program's would be: the feed turns or mirrors for every reader,
and the window follows its size. A still from the shell, without the
window, is
.IR read (1)
of one frame through
.IR i420 (1)
and
.IR topng (1).
.PP
The keys
.B +
and
.B -
move the lens's focus,
.B a
runs autofocus once,
.B s
takes a snapshot, and
.B q
exits.
.PP
With no camera, or when the camera goes, the window stays and says why;
.B q
closes it.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/camera.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR i420 (1),
.IR camsrv (4),
.IR layers (2),
.IR visionfs (4)
.SH BUGS
Resizing the window does not scale the picture, which stays in the
middle of it.
